WEBVTT

00:01.043 --> 00:02.593
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

00:03.793 --> 00:05.076
Tell me, Henry,

00:05.078 --> 00:07.895
why do you want to be
Mr. Schmidt's assistant?

00:07.897 --> 00:09.080
He's my hero.

00:09.082 --> 00:10.665
I know everything about him.

00:11.383 --> 00:14.518
"Possible stalker."

00:15.587 --> 00:17.755
And why do you think
you're qualified?

00:17.757 --> 00:20.141
Like him,
I graduated high school at 16.

00:20.143 --> 00:22.426
Then I completed the four-year
computer science program

00:22.428 --> 00:23.877
at Harvard
in just under two years,

00:23.879 --> 00:26.314
during which,
I founded an Internet startup,

00:26.316 --> 00:29.083
and I'm currently two semesters
shy of my law degree.

00:29.085 --> 00:33.020
So, "no law degree."

00:33.989 --> 00:35.189
Let me tell you a few things

00:35.191 --> 00:36.774
about Walden Schmidt
you may not know.

00:36.776 --> 00:38.075
Uh, the man is a genius.

00:38.077 --> 00:39.860
I knew that.

00:39.862 --> 00:42.896
"Likes to interrupt."

00:43.949 --> 00:46.450
He thinks in a different way
than the rest of us.

00:46.452 --> 00:48.569
His mind is always working.

00:48.571 --> 00:49.920
Every time he opens his mouth,

00:49.922 --> 00:51.622
it's because he has
something important to say.

00:51.624 --> 00:53.341
WALDEN:
Love the new toilet paper

00:53.343 --> 00:54.742
you bought, Alan.

00:54.744 --> 00:56.827
It's like sliding
down a rainbow.

00:57.996 --> 01:00.447
Except the pot at the end
doesn't have any gold in it.

01:00.449 --> 01:01.916
When you hear something
this good,

01:01.918 --> 01:03.384
you should write it down.

01:03.935 --> 01:05.086
I'm sorry.

01:05.088 --> 01:06.170
Who's this?

01:06.172 --> 01:07.672
Oh, this is, uh, Henry Johnson.

01:07.674 --> 01:09.974
He's interviewing
for the assistant job.

01:09.976 --> 01:12.109
Uh, assistant job?

01:12.111 --> 01:13.711
Hi, Mr. Schmidt.

01:13.713 --> 01:15.096
It's such an honor...
(stuttering)

01:15.098 --> 01:17.248
Eye contact.

01:17.250 --> 01:18.632
It's okay, Henry.

01:19.851 --> 01:21.468
(mouthing)

01:22.034 --> 01:23.719
Alan, can I
talk to you for a second.

01:23.744 --> 01:25.393
Uh, no problem,
Mr. Schmidt.

01:27.828 --> 01:29.186
Tie?
Really.

01:29.847 --> 01:31.239
Not looking good, Hank.

01:33.718 --> 01:35.036
What's up?

01:35.037 --> 01:37.771
Why are you interviewing Henry
to be my assistant

01:37.773 --> 01:40.040
when I just hired you
to be my assistant?

01:40.042 --> 01:42.259
Oh, no, no, he's interviewing
to be &lt;i>my&lt;/i> assistant.

01:42.261 --> 01:43.560
Your assistant?

01:43.562 --> 01:44.878
Well, intern, actually.

01:44.880 --> 01:46.747
He's not gonna cost us a penny,
and he's gonna do

01:46.749 --> 01:48.449
all the menial stuff
I don't want to do.

01:48.451 --> 01:50.917
Well, why don't I
just hire him for free

01:50.919 --> 01:52.303
and cut out the middle man?

01:52.305 --> 01:54.688
And in case I'm going too fast,
you're the middle man.

01:54.690 --> 01:56.256
But I'm the big picture guy.

01:56.258 --> 01:58.392
See, bringing Henry
on to Team Schmidt...

01:58.394 --> 02:00.644
Whoa, whoa, whoa!
Team Schmidt?

02:00.646 --> 02:02.146
Yeah, I'm gonna get
hats and shirts made.

02:02.148 --> 02:03.614
Well, Henry is.

02:03.616 --> 02:05.065
We're gonna have a new slogan.

02:05.067 --> 02:07.134
"No bull-Schmidt."

02:08.003 --> 02:10.771
"Schmidt happens."

02:10.773 --> 02:13.240
You're a Schmidt head.

02:15.627 --> 02:18.945
I hired you to be my assistant
to help you out financially

02:18.947 --> 02:20.914
'cause you had close
your chiropractic office.

02:20.916 --> 02:23.083
I didn't have to close it;
I'm in a rent dispute.

02:23.085 --> 02:25.953
People in rent disputes
don't fake their own death.

02:25.955 --> 02:27.738
(doorbell rings)
Oh, I'll get that.

02:27.740 --> 02:29.907
You are looking good today,
boss.

02:29.909 --> 02:31.442
That's why he got
good toilet paper.

02:31.444 --> 02:34.762
So my ass is clean
while he's kissing it.

02:34.764 --> 02:37.398
Huh, my 12:00
must be early.

02:37.400 --> 02:39.983
Someone who really
wanted this job

02:39.985 --> 02:41.185
would've taken the initiative.

02:41.187 --> 02:42.770
Too late, Harvard.

02:45.490 --> 02:47.057
Hello.

02:47.059 --> 02:49.226
Hi. You Alan Harper?

02:49.228 --> 02:51.495
Yes, I am.
And, uh, and you are...?

02:51.497 --> 02:52.496
Your niece.

02:52.498 --> 02:53.864
Eurniece?

02:53.866 --> 02:55.482
That's a...
that's a pretty name.

02:55.484 --> 02:56.583
Is that Dutch?

02:56.585 --> 02:57.951
No, I'm Jenny.

02:57.953 --> 02:59.486
I'm your brother
Charlie's daughter.

02:59.488 --> 03:01.171
Uh, Henry?
Yes?

03:01.173 --> 03:02.489
Catch me.

03:04.342 --> 03:06.427
♪ Men, men, men, men, manly men,
men, men ♪

03:06.429 --> 03:07.557
♪ Ooh
♪ &lt;i>Men. ♪&lt;/i>

03:07.558 --> 03:11.558
&lt;font color="#00FF00">♪ Two and a Half Men 11x01 ♪&lt;/font>
&lt;font color="#00FFFF">Nangnangnangnang&lt;/font>
Original Air Date on September 26, 2013

03:11.561 --> 03:15.561
== sync, corrected by &lt;font color=#00FF00>elderman&lt;/font> ==
&lt;font color=#00FFFF>@elder_man&lt;/font>

03:15.580 --> 03:16.947
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

03:17.149 --> 03:18.982
Uh, I'm-I'm sorry,

03:18.984 --> 03:22.235
did-did you say that
you're... Charlie's daughter?

03:22.237 --> 03:23.904
Yeah.

03:23.906 --> 03:25.338
Listen, I got a wicked hangover.

03:25.340 --> 03:29.793
You got any aspirin, ibuprofen,
rum, Scotch, tequila, vodka?

03:29.795 --> 03:32.078
Uh, yeah, yeah,
come on in.

03:32.080 --> 03:34.581
Uh, Henry, uh,
get her an aspirin and vodka.

03:34.583 --> 03:36.066
On it!

03:36.068 --> 03:38.268
Kitchen's that way.
Damn it!

03:40.905 --> 03:42.305
I-I can't believe this.

03:42.307 --> 03:44.107
I mean, I can, but I-I can't.

03:44.109 --> 03:46.409
I mean, how did this happen?

03:46.411 --> 03:48.011
From what my mom told me...

03:48.013 --> 03:51.782
Ooh, can we... can we maybe
turn down the lights?

03:51.784 --> 03:53.800
That's the sun.

03:53.802 --> 03:55.468
Right, I hate the sun.

03:55.470 --> 03:58.155
It's like God calling you
an alcoholic.

03:59.357 --> 04:02.976
Anyway, according to my mom,
it was love at first sight.

04:02.978 --> 04:04.310
They met in a bar,

04:04.312 --> 04:06.480
they got drunk and had sex
in the bathroom.

04:06.482 --> 04:10.083
(chuckles) It was like
a freakin' Disney movie.

04:11.302 --> 04:14.087
Poke-a-hot-ass.

04:15.823 --> 04:18.341
And where did the kid go
for the vodka? Poland?

04:18.343 --> 04:20.243
Look, I don't mean
to be rude,

04:20.245 --> 04:22.546
but how do I know that you're
really Charlie's daughter?

04:22.548 --> 04:24.631
I mean, this could be
some kind of scam.

04:24.633 --> 04:26.850
I have a picture of us together.

04:26.852 --> 04:28.451
It's in here somewhere.

04:28.453 --> 04:30.437
Oh, look. (laughs)

04:30.439 --> 04:31.721
My vagina.

04:31.723 --> 04:33.990
(chuckles)

04:33.992 --> 04:35.675
Oh, wait, that's not mine.

04:37.328 --> 04:38.845
Oh, that's mine.

04:38.847 --> 04:40.897
(chuckles)

04:40.899 --> 04:42.148
Ah, there you go.

04:42.150 --> 04:44.501
This was taken
at my fourth birthday party.

04:44.503 --> 04:47.654
Just a heads up, I might vomit;
where's the nearest bathroom?

04:47.656 --> 04:48.872
Oh, right down the hall.

04:48.874 --> 04:49.956
Okay, I think we're good,

04:49.958 --> 04:51.358
but it's always nice
to have a plan.

04:51.359 --> 04:54.244
Anyway, this was party was
the last time I saw him.

04:54.246 --> 04:56.046
After that,
he just sent checks.

04:56.048 --> 04:57.697
He-he sent checks?

04:57.699 --> 04:59.883
Yeah, my mom didn't want him
to have anything to do with me,

04:59.885 --> 05:01.751
but he always made sure
I was taken care of.

05:01.753 --> 05:04.203
He never said a word
about any of this to me.

05:04.205 --> 05:06.223
I'm his brother, his-his blood.

05:06.225 --> 05:07.741
Were they big checks?

05:07.743 --> 05:09.676
Yeah, got one every month.

05:09.678 --> 05:11.044
Bastard.

05:11.046 --> 05:14.364
My mom just called me special.

05:14.366 --> 05:15.632
This Henry guy is awesome.

05:15.634 --> 05:18.568
Did you know I won a
spelling bee in fifth grade?

05:20.154 --> 05:22.355
I didn't!

05:24.992 --> 05:27.560
Who's this,
Henry's assistant?

05:27.562 --> 05:30.330
Walden, this is Jenny,

05:30.332 --> 05:32.398
my brother's daughter.

05:32.400 --> 05:34.868
Really?

05:35.770 --> 05:37.787
Hi.
Hi.

05:37.789 --> 05:40.807
I, uh, didn't know
Charlie had a daughter.

05:40.809 --> 05:42.459
Neither did I.

05:42.461 --> 05:45.045
He sent her checks,
big checks.

05:46.047 --> 05:47.764
Not that that matters now.

05:47.766 --> 05:49.349
(whispers):
Every month!

05:50.418 --> 05:52.269
Hey, am I related

05:52.271 --> 05:54.621
to Abercrombie &amp; Fitch
over here?

05:54.623 --> 05:57.757
No, I own the house.

05:57.759 --> 06:00.026
Oh. I assumed it was Alan's.

06:00.028 --> 06:03.063
So does he.

06:03.065 --> 06:05.048
So, uh, tell us
more about you.

06:05.050 --> 06:06.700
Not much to tell.

06:06.702 --> 06:07.901
I was born in New York,

06:07.903 --> 06:09.986
got kicked
out of a few private schools,

06:09.988 --> 06:12.789
tried to become a doctor
to make my mom happy,

06:12.791 --> 06:15.425
dropped out, became an actress
to piss her off.

06:15.427 --> 06:16.826
An actress, oh.

06:16.828 --> 06:18.745
Your father loved actresses.

06:18.747 --> 06:20.714
Yeah, I was only going
to med school

06:20.716 --> 06:22.766
so I could write myself
prescriptions for oxy.

06:22.768 --> 06:25.585
Oh, your father loved oxy.

06:25.587 --> 06:27.437
HENRY:
Sorry it took so long.

06:27.439 --> 06:30.407
Here's vodka and two aspirin.

06:30.409 --> 06:32.625
Thank God. Oh.

06:34.595 --> 06:36.796
I was wrong; I am gonna puke.

06:37.598 --> 06:40.684
Your father
loved to puke.

06:40.686 --> 06:43.136
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

06:43.138 --> 06:44.654
So, when I was, like, five,

06:44.656 --> 06:47.357
my mom married
this total loser named Rob.

06:47.359 --> 06:49.743
He moved in with us
and never looked for a job,

06:49.745 --> 06:51.928
but he's been sponging
off of her ever since.

06:51.930 --> 06:54.147
Who does that?

06:56.500 --> 06:58.635
So, uh, how long
you been in L.A.?

06:58.637 --> 06:59.602
Couple weeks.

06:59.604 --> 07:00.754
And you got a place to stay?

07:00.756 --> 07:03.206
He asks, knowing full well
she's a Harper.

07:03.955 --> 07:07.039
Yeah, I'm crashing
at a friend's house.

07:07.041 --> 07:08.441
That's great. Friends are great.

07:08.443 --> 07:10.710
You should make
some friends, Alan.

07:11.578 --> 07:13.379
So, just the two of you
live here?

07:13.381 --> 07:15.548
Uh, well, my son,
your cousin Jake,

07:15.550 --> 07:18.250
uh, used to live with us,
but he's in the army now.

07:18.252 --> 07:19.368
Stationed in Japan.

07:19.370 --> 07:21.404
Oh, that's impressive.

07:21.406 --> 07:22.605
Because of the time difference,

07:22.607 --> 07:24.874
he thinks he lives
in the future.

07:24.876 --> 07:26.559
Maybe we can call him
and find out

07:26.561 --> 07:28.344
when this headache's
gonna go away.

07:28.346 --> 07:30.363
Oh, and, uh,
you have a grandmother.

07:30.365 --> 07:31.931
Oh, that's great!

07:31.933 --> 07:34.099
In theory.

07:34.101 --> 07:35.768
When she finds out
she has a granddaughter,

07:35.770 --> 07:36.886
she's gonna have a heart attack.

07:36.888 --> 07:39.238
You know,
I'm gonna call her right now.

07:40.457 --> 07:42.274
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

07:42.276 --> 07:43.576
This is it.

07:43.578 --> 07:45.277
This was your dad's room.

07:45.279 --> 07:47.079
Wow.

07:47.081 --> 07:50.716
I always tried to imagine
what my dad's life was like.

07:50.718 --> 07:53.486
It's weird to finally see it.

07:53.488 --> 07:56.255
I never met him,
but I heard he was quite a guy.

07:56.257 --> 07:59.075
I heard he was
a drunken man whore.

07:59.077 --> 08:02.028
Like I said, quite a guy.

08:02.030 --> 08:03.346
So, uh,

08:03.348 --> 08:05.081
this your and Alan's room?

08:05.083 --> 08:06.149
What?

08:06.151 --> 08:07.683
(chuckles):
No.

08:07.685 --> 08:09.318
No, no, no, no, no, no, no.

08:09.320 --> 08:10.820
We're not... I'm not...

08:10.822 --> 08:12.738
The, um... really?

08:12.740 --> 08:15.258
You really don't think
I can do better than Alan?

08:15.260 --> 08:16.609
I don't know.

08:16.611 --> 08:19.479
Maybe he's got a huge schlong.

08:19.481 --> 08:21.981
Well, we're not a couple,
and he doesn't.

08:23.450 --> 08:25.418
Which is fine.
I mean, not that size matters.

08:25.420 --> 08:26.485
Not that I was looking.

08:26.487 --> 08:27.670
I'm not gay.

08:27.672 --> 08:30.990
So why is he still living here?

08:30.992 --> 08:32.675
Well, at first...

08:32.677 --> 08:34.160
Then...

08:34.162 --> 08:35.761
I don't know.

08:36.697 --> 08:38.915
So, um,

08:38.917 --> 08:40.850
this is where your
dad used to sleep.

08:40.852 --> 08:42.468
I got a new mattress,

08:42.470 --> 08:45.087
and I replaced the
carpets and the drapes

08:45.089 --> 08:49.192
and pretty much anything
that could absorb fluid.

08:49.194 --> 08:50.476
Wow.

08:50.478 --> 08:51.677
If these walls could talk.

08:51.679 --> 08:54.764
They'd probably say,
"Can I get a towel?"

08:54.766 --> 08:56.115
So, I mean,

08:56.117 --> 08:58.951
I wish there was more
that Charlie left behind.

08:58.953 --> 09:01.103
You know, other than Alan.

09:01.105 --> 09:03.372
So... (sighs)

09:03.374 --> 09:07.359
my dad stood in this same spot,
staring out at the ocean.

09:07.361 --> 09:09.528
I wonder what was going
through his mind.

09:09.530 --> 09:11.497
I wonder what he was thinking.

09:11.499 --> 09:13.082
Besides, of course,

09:13.084 --> 09:17.053
"how can I nail those two
hot surfer chicks out there?"

09:17.055 --> 09:19.672
Huh, now I'm thinking it.

09:19.674 --> 09:21.591
Oh, please.

09:21.593 --> 09:24.961
With your looks and this house,
I'm sure you do fine.

09:24.963 --> 09:26.946
Well, you'd think that,
but the truth is,

09:26.948 --> 09:29.148
when it comes to women,
I've never really been much

09:29.150 --> 09:30.549
of a casual sex
kind of guy.

09:30.551 --> 09:32.401
And every time I do
get close to one,

09:32.403 --> 09:33.836
she ends up pulling
away from me,

09:33.838 --> 09:35.738
and then I wind up
back in this room,

09:35.740 --> 09:39.058
thinking where I
went wrong again.

09:39.060 --> 09:40.760
Alone.

09:42.429 --> 09:44.630
So alone.

09:46.700 --> 09:48.901
(sighs)

09:49.920 --> 09:51.904
Oh, yeah.

09:51.906 --> 09:54.106
(chuckles)
You're not gay.

09:56.760 --> 09:58.494
Mom, I have some news for you.

09:58.496 --> 10:00.730
Sit down.

10:00.732 --> 10:02.999
Okay, push him off and sit up.

10:03.001 --> 10:06.185
Um, I know this is gonna come
as quite the shock,

10:06.187 --> 10:09.772
but it turns out
Charlie has a daughter.

10:11.091 --> 10:13.809
Mom? Mom?

10:13.811 --> 10:16.212
Are you dead?

10:16.214 --> 10:17.697
Oh, good.

10:17.699 --> 10:19.782
Um, no, I know.

10:19.784 --> 10:21.317
I know, it's crazy, right?

10:21.319 --> 10:23.085
Yeah, no, she's here now.

10:23.087 --> 10:25.071
Well, well, come on over.

10:25.073 --> 10:27.573
Okay, finish first
and then come over.

10:28.942 --> 10:31.327
Good news.
Uh, my mother's on her way over.

10:31.329 --> 10:33.896
First time I've ever said that.

10:33.898 --> 10:36.115
Wow, insta-family.

10:36.117 --> 10:38.117
Uncle, grandmother,

10:38.119 --> 10:39.468
step-hot-guy.

10:39.470 --> 10:41.604
I'm sorry,
I don't know what to call you.

10:41.606 --> 10:43.589
Oh, step-hot-guy works.

10:43.591 --> 10:45.958
All that's missing is my dad.

10:45.960 --> 10:48.511
Actually, he's here, too.

10:48.513 --> 10:50.429
Um, follow me.

10:50.431 --> 10:51.897
Uh, where are we going?

10:51.899 --> 10:53.583
Uh, well, you know how sailors
get buried at sea?

10:53.584 --> 10:54.128
Yeah.

10:54.153 --> 10:56.153
I keep Charlie
in the liquor cabinet.

10:57.821 --> 10:59.471
Let's see.

10:59.473 --> 11:04.026
Uh, Johnnie Walker,
Jack Daniel's...

11:04.028 --> 11:05.695
Charlie Harper.

11:06.730 --> 11:10.333
Huh, he looks different
than his pictures.

11:10.335 --> 11:14.453
Um, Charlie, this is
your daughter Jenny.

11:14.455 --> 11:16.672
Hi, Dad!

11:17.841 --> 11:20.126
This seems weird. Does this
seem weird to anybody else?

11:20.128 --> 11:22.261
Yes, it's weird.

11:22.263 --> 11:26.682
Almost as weird as
when we take him to the movies.

11:29.436 --> 11:31.270
Charlie, I wish you were here

11:31.272 --> 11:34.357
to see how beautiful
your daughter turned out.

11:35.542 --> 11:37.026
I-I think you'd be impressed.

11:37.028 --> 11:38.527
I think a lot of...

11:38.529 --> 11:40.529
Oh!

11:40.531 --> 11:42.298
(coughs)

11:42.300 --> 11:44.884
Oh, not again.

11:44.886 --> 11:47.019
I ain't cleaning that up.

11:55.564 --> 11:57.931
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

12:02.395 --> 12:03.345
Oh. Oh, look.

12:03.346 --> 12:05.179
A quarter.

12:07.716 --> 12:09.266
Unbelievable.

12:09.268 --> 12:11.585
You even mooch
off the dead.

12:12.771 --> 12:13.887
One more.

12:13.889 --> 12:15.922
Yeah, you're
Charlie's daughter.

12:15.924 --> 12:17.558
You don't seem very surprised.

12:17.560 --> 12:20.411
Only surprised there aren't
more of you running around.

12:20.413 --> 12:24.365
God, I loved your dad.

12:24.367 --> 12:26.283
I remember the first
time I met him.

12:26.285 --> 12:28.719
He asked me if I knew
how to do three things:

12:28.721 --> 12:30.788
cook, clean and
score an eight ball

12:30.790 --> 12:32.623
at 2:30 in the morning.

12:33.892 --> 12:36.960
I told him I didn't know
how to cook or clean.

12:36.962 --> 12:38.612
I've been here ever since.

12:38.614 --> 12:40.113
(laughs)

12:40.115 --> 12:42.416
I'm-I'm sure you have
a story about Charlie

12:42.418 --> 12:43.701
that doesn't involve drugs.

12:43.703 --> 12:47.004
Okay. One time
at Mardi Gras...

12:47.006 --> 12:48.505
Or alcohol.

12:48.507 --> 12:49.923
All right.

12:49.925 --> 12:51.942
Once when Charlie
was in Vegas...

12:51.944 --> 12:53.894
Or hookers.

12:53.896 --> 12:56.980
Geez, you're really
tying my hands!

12:58.083 --> 12:59.083
Okay, I got it.

12:59.085 --> 13:01.034
It was New Year's Eve,

13:01.036 --> 13:03.704
and Charlie was
super not drunk,

13:03.706 --> 13:06.724
and he was with this
crazy not hooker,

13:06.726 --> 13:10.043
and he decided to have
his sphincter bleached.

13:10.045 --> 13:11.995
Whoa! Whoa!
What?

13:11.997 --> 13:12.963
Why?

13:12.965 --> 13:15.499
Because he cared
about women.

13:16.684 --> 13:20.671
Unfortunately, it got
infected, and he needed me

13:20.673 --> 13:23.757
(voice breaks): to dab
a little ointment...

13:23.759 --> 13:25.626
I'm sorry.

13:25.628 --> 13:28.112
It's just that I miss him
so much!

13:28.114 --> 13:30.848
God took the wrong Harper!

13:31.883 --> 13:33.851
(door closes)

13:33.853 --> 13:36.353
EVELYN:
Where is my granddaughter?

13:36.355 --> 13:38.439
Did it just get cold in here?

13:39.624 --> 13:42.392
Oh, my God.

13:42.394 --> 13:44.010
Look at you.

13:44.012 --> 13:45.562
Mom, this is Jenny.

13:45.564 --> 13:46.613
Jenny,

13:46.615 --> 13:48.232
this is Evelyn.

13:48.234 --> 13:50.033
You are so beautiful.

13:50.035 --> 13:52.369
You remind me of me
ten years ago.

13:53.955 --> 13:56.290
Your father was
the apple of my eye.

13:56.292 --> 13:57.791
My greatest gift.

13:57.793 --> 13:59.460
My reason for living.

14:00.311 --> 14:01.361
Uh, hello.

14:02.247 --> 14:04.047
Hello, Alan.

14:05.032 --> 14:09.336
I can't believe
I finally have a grandchild.

14:09.338 --> 14:11.221
You already have
a grandchild-- Jake.

14:11.223 --> 14:14.475
Oh. Sure. Yeah.

14:15.543 --> 14:17.561
So, Jennifer...

14:17.563 --> 14:18.829
Actually, it's Jenny.

14:18.831 --> 14:21.815
Darling, you're not 12 anymore.
It's Jennifer.

14:21.817 --> 14:24.318
We are going to have
so much fun together:

14:24.320 --> 14:28.806
lunching, shopping,
taking care of those eyebrows.

14:28.808 --> 14:30.407
Where are you staying
while you're in town?

14:30.409 --> 14:32.176
I'm crashing on
a friend's couch.

14:32.178 --> 14:34.545
Not anymore.
You'll stay with me.

14:34.547 --> 14:36.947
Aw! I love you, Evelyn.

14:36.949 --> 14:38.248
Whoa, whoa!
If she's staying anywhere,

14:38.250 --> 14:39.433
she's gonna stay at my place.

14:39.435 --> 14:41.451
And by "your place," do you mean

14:41.453 --> 14:44.121
the office that
you stopped paying rent at

14:44.123 --> 14:46.673
or the house that
you've never paid rent at?

14:46.675 --> 14:48.759
Look, I'm not gonna let my mom
screw her up

14:48.761 --> 14:50.010
like she did me and Charlie.

14:50.012 --> 14:52.679
Hey! I was a good mother.

14:52.681 --> 14:54.381
No, you know
who was a good mother?

14:54.383 --> 14:56.466
Our housekeeper Adela.
She even breast-fed me.

14:56.468 --> 14:59.102
She had just had a baby.

14:59.104 --> 15:01.305
And when the milk truck
is parked on the street,

15:01.307 --> 15:03.273
you don't go
to the grocery store.

15:04.292 --> 15:08.228
Besides, you-you used
to gnaw on me.

15:09.113 --> 15:10.731
You're gnawer.

15:10.733 --> 15:12.432
Nang-nang-nang-nang-
nang-nang-nang.

15:12.434 --> 15:15.485
You know what?
She's gonna stay in Jake's room.

15:15.487 --> 15:17.237
Whoa, whoa, no.

15:17.239 --> 15:19.873
I do not want Jake's room
to become Jenny's room.

15:19.875 --> 15:22.159
You know, in fact,
there is no Jake's room

15:22.161 --> 15:23.293
and there's no Jenny's room.

15:23.295 --> 15:24.945
There's just Walden's room.

15:24.947 --> 15:27.764
And Charlie's room.

15:27.766 --> 15:29.650
Why don't we let her decide?

15:29.652 --> 15:30.801
Yeah, yeah,
it's up to her.

15:30.803 --> 15:33.503
Is anyone listening to me?!

15:33.505 --> 15:35.405
Jennifer?

15:35.407 --> 15:36.757
Where'd she go?

15:38.927 --> 15:40.227
Nice job, Alan.

15:40.229 --> 15:43.096
You made another woman
disappear.

15:43.098 --> 15:44.297
Can you believe her?

15:44.299 --> 15:46.550
What did I do to her to
make her hate me so much?

15:46.552 --> 15:48.518
Nang-nang-nang-nang-
nang-nang-nang.

15:48.520 --> 15:51.405
Oh, oh. What, you, too?

15:51.407 --> 15:53.974
Oh!

15:53.976 --> 15:55.909
Son of a...

15:55.911 --> 15:57.744
Ooh, a nickel!

15:57.746 --> 15:59.446
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

15:59.448 --> 16:01.198
This is ridiculous.

16:01.200 --> 16:02.449
We're never going to find her.

16:02.451 --> 16:04.484
I don't understand
why she ran off like that.

16:04.486 --> 16:06.253
I can think of two reasons.

16:09.123 --> 16:12.826
First I lost my Charlie,
now I've lost my Jennifer.

16:12.828 --> 16:14.511
You still have your Alan.

16:14.513 --> 16:17.014
Oh! Don't make it worse.

16:18.332 --> 16:20.017
Nang-nang-nang-nang-
nang-nang-nang.

16:21.619 --> 16:25.555
Oh, God,
my granddaughter's gone forever.

16:25.557 --> 16:28.392
Oh, there she is
at the bus stop.

16:28.394 --> 16:32.329
Oh, God, my granddaughter
rides the bus!

16:37.035 --> 16:38.869
Jenny, what are you doing?

16:38.871 --> 16:41.438
I'm trying to get away
from you people.

16:41.440 --> 16:43.290
Look, I just wanted to see
where my dad lived.

16:43.292 --> 16:44.925
I didn't want
to screw up your family.

16:44.927 --> 16:46.043
Uh, for the record,

16:46.045 --> 16:47.878
they were screwed up
long before you got here.

16:47.880 --> 16:49.129
It's true.

16:49.131 --> 16:51.048
H-Hey, if I'm screwed up,
it's your fault.

16:51.050 --> 16:51.999
You raised me.

16:52.001 --> 16:54.434
I didn't raise you,
Adela did.

16:54.436 --> 16:57.504
Look, I already have
a messed-up family.

16:57.506 --> 16:58.922
I-I don't need another one.

16:58.924 --> 16:59.923
Oh, we're sorry.

16:59.925 --> 17:01.825
This is just how
we express our love.

17:01.827 --> 17:03.927
Through hate.
Oh, no, no, no.

17:03.929 --> 17:05.262
W-We don't hate each other.

17:05.264 --> 17:09.833
I mean, the truth is,
my mother is an amazing woman.

17:09.835 --> 17:11.868
I mean, she-she raised
two kids on her own,

17:11.870 --> 17:13.820
she's a successful
businesswoman,

17:13.822 --> 17:17.074
she has impeccable taste.

17:17.076 --> 17:18.391
Thank you, Alan.

17:19.694 --> 17:20.744
Oh, right.

17:20.746 --> 17:23.697
Uh, and Alan is...

17:23.699 --> 17:26.950
the reason I had
my tubes tied.

17:28.052 --> 17:31.455
Because she knew she would
never do better than me.

17:32.690 --> 17:36.460
Please, sweetheart,
I just found you.

17:36.462 --> 17:37.511
I can't lose you now.

17:37.513 --> 17:39.546
We want you to be a
part of our lives.

17:39.548 --> 17:40.630
What do you say?

17:40.632 --> 17:43.750
Well, if I'm gonna be
a part of this family,

17:43.752 --> 17:45.602
I'm gonna need a drink.

17:45.604 --> 17:47.054
You hear that, Charlie?

17:47.056 --> 17:48.722
Your daughter
needs a drink.

17:48.724 --> 17:51.441
You're looking the
wrong way, Mom.

17:51.443 --> 17:53.377
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

17:54.562 --> 17:56.429
A toast.
To Charlie Harper.

17:56.431 --> 18:00.384
My brother, your son,
your father, and your...

18:00.386 --> 18:03.236
Guy who got hit by a train
so I could buy his beach house?

18:04.288 --> 18:05.238
Sorry, Evelyn.

18:05.240 --> 18:07.007
It's okay. I got the commission.

18:07.009 --> 18:09.993
To Charlie.

18:09.995 --> 18:13.130
So, is that the bathroom

18:13.132 --> 18:15.415
where the miracle
of my life began?

18:16.667 --> 18:18.001
It is.

18:19.504 --> 18:20.470
Want to see it?

18:20.472 --> 18:21.671
I do.

18:21.673 --> 18:23.473
Text a picture of it to my mom.

18:23.475 --> 18:25.425
Should be good
for some guilt money.

18:25.427 --> 18:27.627
I'll run interference.

18:29.013 --> 18:30.147
All right, everybody out!

18:30.149 --> 18:32.632
Woman visiting the place
of her conception!

18:34.168 --> 18:36.236
I can't tell you
how relieved I am

18:36.238 --> 18:38.405
to finally have an heir.
Mm.

18:38.407 --> 18:39.423
Wait, what?

18:39.425 --> 18:41.191
She's my granddaughter.

18:41.193 --> 18:43.143
I want to provide
for her.

18:43.145 --> 18:44.578
And since I wasn't around

18:44.580 --> 18:46.696
for the first 25 years
of her life,

18:46.698 --> 18:48.949
it's only fitting that
she inherit my estate.

18:48.951 --> 18:51.317
You weren't around for
the first 45 years of my life.

18:51.319 --> 18:53.170
You have Walden!

18:53.172 --> 18:55.472
Oh, oh, do I? Do you see
a ring on this finger?

18:55.474 --> 18:56.823
Don't worry, darling.

18:56.825 --> 18:59.209
There's a little something
for you in my will.

18:59.211 --> 19:00.043
A little something?

19:00.045 --> 19:01.261
Look, if you knew

19:01.263 --> 19:02.879
you were gonna
get everything,

19:02.881 --> 19:05.265
you would've smothered me
with a pillow years ago.

19:05.267 --> 19:06.616
That is not true.

19:06.618 --> 19:10.353
If I knew I had money coming,
I'd hire a professional.

19:11.773 --> 19:13.557
How'd it go?
Great.

19:13.559 --> 19:15.192
I laughed, I cried.

19:15.194 --> 19:18.161
I peed.

19:18.163 --> 19:19.930
How are you guys doing
over here?

19:19.932 --> 19:21.481
Can I get you anything else?

19:23.434 --> 19:25.535
Yeah, we might need
a designated driver

19:25.537 --> 19:27.988
to get us back
to his beautiful beach house.

19:29.023 --> 19:31.158
I'll take you guys.
I get off in 15.

19:32.493 --> 19:34.044
Great. Thanks.

19:36.247 --> 19:37.697
She's cute.

19:37.699 --> 19:38.799
Told ya.

19:38.801 --> 19:42.002
Malibu beach house
gets you laid every time.

19:42.687 --> 19:45.005
Not every time.

19:46.674 --> 19:49.176
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

19:49.178 --> 19:52.562
Oh, my God,
this house is amazing!

19:52.564 --> 19:54.798
Well, it's... Yeah.

19:54.800 --> 19:57.517
And look at
that view.

19:57.519 --> 19:59.269
It's even better
from the bedroom.

19:59.271 --> 20:00.353
Want to see?

20:00.355 --> 20:01.538
Yeah.

20:01.540 --> 20:03.073
After you.

20:04.041 --> 20:05.542
Whoa, whoa, whoa,
whoa, whoa.

20:05.544 --> 20:06.710
Where are you going?

20:06.712 --> 20:07.878
Up to show her.

20:07.880 --> 20:09.830
Oh, you thought...?

20:09.832 --> 20:12.532
Oh, no-no-no-no-no,
she's mine.

20:12.534 --> 20:14.400
Next time I'll get two.

20:18.956 --> 20:21.408
What just happened?

20:21.410 --> 20:23.243
Charlie's back.

20:23.245 --> 20:25.745
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

20:31.831 --> 20:33.949
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

20:33.951 --> 20:34.917
Good morning.

20:34.919 --> 20:36.352
No, no, not good.

20:36.354 --> 20:38.287
I slept in the guest room
of my own house,

20:38.289 --> 20:41.690
and I'm pretty sure I still have
some of your brother in my ear.

20:41.692 --> 20:43.092
Don't worry,
tonight I'll tell Jenny

20:43.094 --> 20:44.293
that your bedroom's off limits.

20:44.295 --> 20:45.561
No, there is no tonight!

20:45.563 --> 20:46.562
But she's family.

20:46.564 --> 20:47.763
Not my family.

20:47.765 --> 20:49.882
And I'm gonna tell her
she can't stay.

20:50.734 --> 20:52.718
Morning.
Hi.

20:52.720 --> 20:53.969
You girls have a good night?

20:53.971 --> 20:55.804
Oh, yeah.

20:56.252 --> 20:59.170
I'm surprised I can even talk.

21:01.208 --> 21:03.759
You were saying?
Shut up.

21:03.761 --> 21:08.761
== sync, corrected by &lt;font color=#00FF00>elderman&lt;/font> ==
&lt;font color=#00FFFF>@elder_man&lt;/font>

21:42.666 --> 21:44.586
(bell tolling)
PRIEST: We commend to Almighty God
